# BBN exclusion of a single Majorana HNL, |U_{\tau N}|^2 single-flavour mixing
# Source: Chen and Zhang, 'BBN constraint on heavy neutrino production and decay',
#   arXiv:2410.07343v2 (Phys. Rev. D 111 (2025) 123024), Fig. 8 (bottom): the blue 'BBN Constraint' region.
# Source figure PDF: sources/arXiv-2410.07343/Utau4sq_constraints.pdf (arXiv source bundle)
# Model: one Majorana heavy neutrino mixing with a single active flavour, whose
#   abundance (thermal freeze-out, or freeze-in from zero) and decays are both fixed
#   by (m_N, |U|^2) -- the paper's benchmark. Excluded at 95% CL (Y_p and D/H).
#   Used as published: no CL rescaling, no Dirac/Majorana factor.
# Method: vector extraction of the region's two solid navy boundary strokes,
#   RGB(0,0,0.502), each checked to lie on the outline of its 30%-opacity fill;
#   log-axis calibration from TICK GEOMETRY:
#   x 200.3605 pt/decade (major ticks 1e-3 .. 10, 30 GeV; fit residual 0.000 pt),
#   y 19.7295 pt/decade (a major tick every decade, 10^0 .. 10^-28).
# Coverage: m_N = 0.001 .. 1.2 GeV (top), 0.001 .. 1.2 GeV (bottom).
#   The paper's region ends at m_N = 1.2 GeV with a dashed closure (top edge there
#   1.91e-11): its calculation stops, leaving 1-10 GeV as a gap. That closure
#   is not stored, nor are the >= 10 GeV region and, above 0.3 GeV, the CMB constraint,
#   both below |U|^2 = 1e-15.
#   The top edge crosses |U|^2 = 1e-10 at m_N = 0.775 GeV.
#   The paper draws each boundary as a coarse polygon: the top edge has 6 vertices
#   from 0.3 to 1.2 GeV, and is stored as drawn.
# top = upper boundary (the HNL decays too early, tau ~ 0.02 s); bottom = lower
#   boundary (too little abundance). The region between them is excluded.
# Extracted: 2026-09-28
# mass_GeV  U2
